/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 93 0 R
/T (The digital twin maintains a virtual representation of the campus and its interconnected resources, allowing proposed changes to be tested before they are implemented physically. A user can propose a scenario such as moving students between laboratories, changing classroom allocations, increasing student intake, modifying bus schedules, or temporarily closing a facility. CampusTwin applies the proposed change to the digital model and evaluates its predicted effects on utilization, capacity, energy consumption, scheduling conflicts, transportation demand, and other dependent resources. This allows administrators to experiment with different scenarios without disrupting the real campus.)
/E (The digital twin maintains a virtual representation of the campus and its interconnected resources, allowing proposed changes to be tested before they are implemented physically. A user can propose a scenario such as moving students between laboratories, changing classroom allocations, increasing student intake, modifying bus schedules, or temporarily closing a facility. CampusTwin applies the proposed change to the digital model and evaluates its predicted effects on utilization, capacity, energy consumption, scheduling conflicts, transportation demand, and other dependent resources. This allows administrators to experiment with different scenarios without disrupting the real campus.)
