<<
/Title (CampusTwin continues to evolve after a decision is implemented by comparing predicted outcomes with what actually happens on campus. For example, if the twin predicts that moving a class will increase laboratory utilization to 78%, the actual utilization after implementation can be measured and compared against that prediction. These differences become feedback for improving future analysis and predictive models. Over time, the system develops a more accurate understanding of the specific campus, allowing its simulations and recommendations to become increasingly reliable. This creates a continuous loop of simulate, implement, observe, learn, and improve.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 224 0 R
>>
